  "description": "Reid Explorer S 16\" | Kids BMX-style bike\nBuilt for little riders with big imaginations, the Reid Bikes Explorer S 16\" kids' bike is a fun, easy-to-ride bike with BMX-inspired styling and practical features to help young cyclists build confidence.\nDesigned for children aged approximately 4–8 years, the Reid Bikes Explorer S 16\" features a durable steel frame and BMX-style handlebars for a comfortable, controlled riding position. Its junior-specific saddle and grips are sized for smaller riders, helping make every ride more comfortable.\nThe 16-inch alloy wheels are fitted with wide 2.35\" tyres, providing stability and grip for riding around the park, on paths and during everyday adventures. A singlespeed drivetrain keeps things simple, allowing children to focus on developing their balance and riding skills without worrying about changing gears.\nA rear coaster brake allows riders to slow down by pedalling backwards, while a front V-brake provides additional stopping control. The full-length chainguard helps protect clothing and little hands from the chain, and detachable training wheels offer extra support while children develop their confidence.\nFinished in eye-catching hot pink, the Reid Bikes Explorer S 16\" combines playful BMX styling with a straightforward design that makes learning to ride enjoyable.\nThe Reid Bikes Explorer S 16\" kids' bike is ideal for:\n\nYoung first-time cyclists, with a simple singlespeed setup that's easy to use\n\nBuilding riding confidence, with detachable training wheels for additional support\n\nStable everyday riding, with 16-inch alloy wheels and wide 2.35\" tyres\n\nEasy braking, with a rear coaster brake and front V-brake\n\nComfort for smaller riders, with junior-specific handlebars, grips and saddle\n\nAdded protection, with a full-length chainguard to help keep clothing and hands clear of the chain\n\nGrowing independence, with a durable steel frame and BMX-inspired design",
